@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/{id}/versions/{version} — fetch one full team version
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Team owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.getVersion(id, version)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nread node" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> SDK : getVersion(id, version)
SDK -> API : GET /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/{id}/versions/{version}
API -> Domain : get(address, id, version)
Domain -> Chain : explore-deploy get.rho
alt the version exists
  Chain --> Domain : full record
  Domain --> API : AgentsTeam { ..., graph?, definition? }
  API --> SDK : 200 AgentsTeam\n(graph parsed to a typed AST by the SDK)
  SDK --> Owner : team incl. both serializations
else unknown address, id, or version
  Chain --> Domain : nothing
  API <-- Domain : not found
  SDK <-- API : 404, no body
end

note over Domain #FFF0C7
A team version carries up to two serializations
of one drawing: the legacy graphl graph (TOGL
term algebra) and the Workflow v2 definition
(statechart semantics). Deploy prefers the
definition and falls back to the graph.
end note
@enduml
